# Commits

Spec: https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/

- Ask the user before `git commit`, amend, or rebase. Show the message and the files. Wait.
- Skip asking only after they explicitly allow it for this conversation.
- One logical unit per commit. It should typecheck on its own.
- Update docs in the same commit as the behaviour they describe.
- Never commit secrets, `.env*` (except `.env.example`), `node_modules`, or `.next`.
- Do not push unless asked.

```
<type>(<scope>): <imperative summary, lowercase, no period>

Refs: U3.2
```

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `refactor`, `test`, `chore`, `build`, `ci`, `perf`, `style`, `revert`.

Scopes: `contracts`, `mocks`, `tokens`, `ui-kit`, `home`, `run`, `runs`, `airwallex`, `csv`, `demo`, `webhooks`, `db`, `docs`, `rules`, `config`, `deps`.

```
feat(ui-kit): add contractor row states for the review gate

Refs: U3.3
```
